  "main_judgment": "The event differences are mechanically real, but the first divergence, current exposure, current wealth and historical peak play different roles on different paths. No single explanation based on greater equity exposure, fewer trades or lower wealth covers all five model-only crossing occurrences. Historical peak dependence explains how an account can have higher wealth yet greater maximum drawdown, without a reset bug. This does not identify which forecast or learning assumption caused the complete policy difference.",
