  "control_98": "Full M and full own-target B both first cross inyear21. The own-inner M and own-inner B both remain below40%. This disappearance is consistent with a different learned target/fan/state trajectory, not disappearance of an invalid market ID. The market remains in every denominator.",
  "mathematical_identities": {
    "log_growth": "Annual real-log-growth gap = log(1-feeM/VM)-log(1-feeB/VB)+log(gM)-log(gB); g is the post-fee portfolio gross factor. Common inflation cancels exactly. The two terms telescope to the terminal log wealth ratio.",
    "nominal_direct": "End nominal wealth gap = start nominal wealth gap - current nominal fee gap + sum(asset_return * posttrade_holding_gap).",
    "nominal_ordered": "Equivalently: start_gap*gB -(feeM-feeB)*gB +(VM-feeM)*(gM-gB). This ordered three-term identity and the direct P&L identity are alternatives, never terms to add together. The ordering convention is not unique causal attribution.",
    "current_drawdown": "DDM-DDB=(RB-RM)/PB+RM*(1/PB-1/PM). The two terms add for CURRENT drawdown only, not lifetime running MDD. Each arm running MDD remains the maximum of its entire own DD history.",
    "fees": "Qg already includes current and future branch fees. Summing nonoverlapping realized annual log-fee differences is valid accounting; summing overlapping state forecast-Q gaps as realized cumulative loss is invalid."
  },
  "what_is_and_is_not_established": {
    "established": [
      "Exact original-ID/job/target pairing for every saved account.",
      "Copied recorded Q score arithmetic and original action consistency; actual fee/holdings/CPI/peak/MDD/pending history matches an independent replay.",
      "All11paired paths and30years retained; full/inner/outer account scopes kept distinct.",
      "MDD event differences and their crossing-year current-DD ratio identities are observed in fixed supplied scenarios."
    ],
    "not_established": [
      "No recalibration or validation of the unconditional calendar fan as a conditional market law.",
      "No separation of forecast error, sampling, selection, target or technical-price causal contributions.",
      "No proof that changing the first differing action improves risk or growth; that is a separate fixed intervention question.",
      "No population-risk estimate, extra independent sample, safety guarantee or newly approved strategy."
    ]
  },
